        "original_id": "24bdff96-2416-546a-9558-d3a068dcb75c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Great War (documentary)\n- Organizations: Imperial War Museum, British Broadcasting Corporation, Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, Australian Broadcasting Commission, Imperial War Museums\n- People: Michael Redgrave, Marius Goring, Ralph Richardson, Cyril Luckham, Sebastian Shaw, Emlyn Williams\n- Topics: First World War\n\nFacts:\n- The Great War is a 26-episode documentary series from 1964 about the First World War.\n- The Great War was co-produced by the Imperial War Museum, the British Broadcasting Corporation, the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, and the Australian Broadcasting Commission.\n- Michael Redgrave was the narrator of The Great War.\n- Marius Goring, Ralph Richardson, Cyril Luckham, Sebastian Shaw, and Emlyn Williams provided readings for The Great War.\n- Imperial War Museums is a British national museum organisation with branches at five locations in England, including three in London.",
